.TH "removeNode" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
removeNode \- remove the specified node in the replication group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]rg.removeNode(<hostname>, <svcname>, [options])\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
SdbReplicaGroup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to remove the specified node in the current replication
group.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \[bu] 2
hostname ( \f[I]string, required\f[] )
.RS 2
.PP
Host name.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
svcname ( \f[I]number/string, required\f[] )
.RS 2
.PP
Node port name.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
options ( \f[I]object, optional\f[] )
.RS 2
.PP
Set the optional parameter through the parameter "options":
.PP
Enforced ( \f[I]boolean\f[] )：Whether to forcibly remove the node, and the
default value is "false", which means that the node is not forcibly removed.
.IP \[bu] 2
When there are multiple nodes in the replication group, if the user needs to
remove the primary node, the user needs to specify "Enforced" as "true".
.IP \[bu] 2
If the user needs to remove the only empty node in the group, the user needs to
specify "Enforced" as "true".
.PP
Format: \f[C]Enforced: true\f[]
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
